# Root ignores
*.pem
*.key
# Apple hands you the Sign in with Apple signing key as a .p8, and
# backend/.env.example tells the operator to open one. It authenticates the
# whole Apple integration, and *.pem / *.key do not cover that extension.
*.p8
secrets/
# Real environment files, anywhere in the tree. backend/.gitignore covered
# backend/.env only, so deploy/.env.production -- which holds the database
# password, the JWT signing key and the Apple private key -- was committable.
# The .example files are the ones meant to be tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
# Database dumps taken before destructive cleanups. Local only -- they
# contain every account and price in the database.
backups/
